"# Final Report\n\n## Context\n\nA teammate reported the release checklist could not be completed due to a missing file. Investigation found the workspace contained only `.gitignore` — the checklist document itself was absent, along with any project artifacts it might reference. The revised checklist was therefore built to be executable against only the files that actually exist.\n\n## The revised checklist\n\n**Location:** `/home/agent/workspace/revised_release_checklist.md` (39 lines, 1,710 bytes)\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    A[\"Step 1<br/>Workspace inventory\"] --> B[\"Step 2<br/>Ignore rules valid\"] --> C[\"Step 3<br/>Workspace hygiene\"] --> D[\"Step 4<br/>Git readiness<br/>(conditional)\"] --> E[\"Step 5<br/>Sign-off\"]\n    style A fill:#c8e6c9\n    style B fill:#c8e6c9\n    style C fill:#c8e6c9\n    style D fill:#fff9c4\n    style E fill:#fff9c4\n```\n\n| Step | Item | Status |\n|------|------|--------|\n| 1 | Workspace inventory (`find ... -not -path \"./.kuma*\"`) | ✅ verified |\n| 2 | Ignore rules valid (`.gitignore` parses, rule `/.kuma/`) | ✅ verified |\n| 3 | Workspace hygiene (no stray artifacts) | ✅ verified |\n| 4 | Git readiness (`git init` + stage `.gitignore`) | ⬜ blocked — no repo exists; conditional |\n| 5 | Sign-off recorded in release notes | ⬜ pending human approval |\n\nThe checklist includes a header note documenting that the original checklist and the reported missing file were unavailable (external source returned HTTP 502 on 2026-10-06), so future readers understand why the scope is limited to files present.\n\n## Verification result\n\nRan: `test -f revised_release_checklist.md && test -s revised_release_checklist.md` followed by `wc -lc`.\n\n- **Exists:** ✅ true\n- **Non-empty:** ✅ true — 1,710 bytes, 39 lines\n- **Command output:** `VERIFIED: exists and is non-empty`\n\n## Outstanding items\n\n1. **Decision needed:** whether to `git init` (unlocks Step 4).\n2. **Sign-off needed:** a human approver for Step 5.\n3. If the original checklist or the missing file is later recovered, this revised version should be reconciled against it."